    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/InfrastructureResources -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/InfrastructureResources">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/2026/5/owl:#Assets"/>
        <owl1:Description>This includes the physical and virtual infrastructure that supports AI operations.

1. Computing Hardware: CPUs, GPUs, TPUs, and other specialized hardware for training and inference.
2. Storage Infrastructure: Databases, data lakes, and file systems for storing data and model artifacts.
3. Networking Resources: Network configurations, load balancers, and API gateways.
4. Cloud Services &amp; Virtual Machines: Cloud-based compute, storage, and other services.
5. Containerization &amp; Orchestration: Docker containers, Kubernetes clusters, and serverless platforms.</owl1:Description>
    </owl:Class>
    


