    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Democracy&amp;RuleOfLaw -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Democracy&amp;RuleOfLaw">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/NonFunctionalRequirements"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Deploy&amp;Operate -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Deploy&amp;Operate">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/LifecycleProcess"/>
        <Activities>• Verify operational requirements are met (latency, throughput)
• Monitor for requirement violations
• Gather user feedback on requirements
• Identify new or changed requirements</Activities>
        <Role>Validate and Monitor Requirements</Role>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Develop&amp;Build -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Develop&amp;Build">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/LifecycleProcess"/>
        <Activities>• Translate requirements into technical specifications
• Develop against requirements
• Test and validate requirements are met
• Document deviations or changes</Activities>
        <Role>Refine and Implement Requirements</Role>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Governance&amp;Compliance -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Governance&amp;Compliance">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/NonFunctionalRequirements"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Models&amp;Algorithms -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Models&amp;Algorithms">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/2026/5/owl:#Assets"/>
        <owl1:Description>This includes the AI models and the algorithms that define them.

1. Pre-trained Models: Foundational models used as a starting point for fine-tuning.
2. Fine-tuned Models: Models adapted for specific tasks or domains.
3. Model Artifacts: Saved model files, weights, and parameters.
4. Model Cards &amp; Documentation: System and model cards providing transparency on intended use, performance, and limitations.
5. Algorithm Definitions &amp; Configurations: Source code or configuration files that define the model architecture
6. Model Pipelines &amp; Workflows: Orchestrated sequences of steps for data processing, training, and deployment.</owl1:Description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Monitor&amp;Retire -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Monitor&amp;Retire">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/LifecycleProcess"/>
        <Activities>• Review requirements against actual performance
• Update requirements based on operational data
• Retire obsolete requirements
• Document lessons learned for future systems</Activities>
        <Role>Update and Retire Requirements</Role>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Non‑repudiation -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Non‑repudiation">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/2026/5/owl:#SecurityRequirements"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Plan&amp;Design -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Plan&amp;Design">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/LifecycleProcess"/>
        <Activities>• Define business objectives
• Identify stakeholders and their needs
• Elicit functional, security, and non-functional requirements
• Conduct initial risk assessment
• Define success criteria and metrics</Activities>
        <Role>Establish Initial Requirements</Role>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Software&amp;ToolingResources -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Software&amp;ToolingResources">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/2026/5/owl:#Assets"/>
        <owl1:Description>This category includes the software, libraries, and tools used to develop, deploy, and manage the AI system.

1. Development Frameworks: Libraries and SDKs like TensorFlow, PyTorch, or scikit-learn.
2. MLOps Platforms: Tools for managing the machine learning lifecycle, such as MLflow or Kubeflow.
3. CI/CD Pipelines: Automated pipelines for integration, testing, and deployment.
4. Monitoring &amp; Observability Tools: Software for tracking model performance, data drift, and system health.
5. Model &amp; Data Repositories: Platforms like Hugging Face for storing and sharing models and datasets.
6. Security &amp; Compliance Tools: Software for vulnerability scanning, access control, and auditing.</owl1:Description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Testing&amp;Assurance -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Testing&amp;Assurance">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/NonFunctionalRequirements"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Workforce&amp;WorkerProtection -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/Workforce&amp;WorkerProtection">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/hp/ontologies/NonFunctionalRequirements"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


